.Sh DESCRIPTION
The Time-Stamp Protocol (TSP) is defined by RFC 3161. TSP is a protocol
used to provide long-term proof of the existence of certain data before
a particular time.
TSP defines a Time Stamping Authority (TSA) and an entity that makes
requests to the TSA. Usually, the TSA is referred to as the server side,
and the requesting entity is referred to as the client.
.Pp
In TSP, when a server sends a response to a client, the server normally
needs to sign the response data - the TimeStampToken (TST) - with its
private key.
Then the client verifies the received TST using the server's certificate
chain.
.Pp
For all the following methods, unless noted otherwise,
.Fa ctx
is the verification context created in advance.
.Pp
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_new
returns an allocated
.Vt TS_VERIFY_CTX
structure.
.Pp
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_init
initializes a verification context.
.Pp
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_free
frees up a
.Vt TS_VERIFY_CTX
object.
.Fa ctx
is the verification context to be freed.
If
.Fa ctx
is NULL, the call is ignored.
.Pp
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_set_flags
sets the flags in the verification context.
.Fa f
are the flags to be set.
.Pp
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_add_flags
adds flags to the verification context.
.Fa f
are the flags to be added (OR'd).
.Pp
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_set0_data
sets the data to be verified.
.Fa b
is the
.Vt BIO
with the data.
A previously assigned
.Vt BIO
is freed.
.Pp
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_set0_imprint
sets the message imprint.
.Fa hexstr
is the message imprint to be assigned.
A previously assigned imprint is freed.
.Pp
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_set0_store
sets the store for the verification context.
.Fa s
is the store to be assigned.
A previously assigned store is freed.
.Pp
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_set0_certs
is used to set the server's certificate chain when verifying a TST.
.Fa certs
is a stack of
.Sy X509
certificates.
.Pp
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_cleanup
frees all data associated with the given
.Vt TS_VERIFY_CTX
object and initializes it.
.Fa ctx
is the verification context created in advance.
If
.Fa ctx
is NULL, the call is ignored.
.Pp
All of the following functions described are deprecated.
Applications should instead use the functions
.Xr TS_VERIFY_CTX_set0_data 3 ,
.Xr TS_VERIFY_CTX_set0_imprint 3 ,
.Xr TS_VERIFY_CTX_set0_store 3 ,
.Xr TS_VERIFY_CTX_set0_certs 3 .
.Pp
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_set_data
is used to set the BIO with the data to be verified.
A previously assigned BIO is
.Sy not freed
by this call.
.Fa b
is the
.Vt BIO
with the data to assign.
.Pp
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_set_imprint
is used to set the message imprint.
A previously assigned imprint
.Sy is freed
by this call.
.Fa hexstr
is the string with the message imprint to assign.
.Pp
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_set_store
is used to set the certificate store.
A previously assigned store is
.Sy not freed
by this call.
.Fa s
is the store to assign.
.Pp
.Xr TS_VERIFY_CTX_set_certs 3
is used to set the server's certificate chain.
A previously assigned stack is
.Sy not freed
by this call.
.Fa certs
is a stack of
.Sy X509
certificates.
.Pp
.Xr TS_VERIFY_CTS_set_certs 3
is a misspelled version of
.Xr TS_VERIFY_CTX_set_certs 3
which takes the same parameters and returns the same result.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_new
returns an allocated
.Vt TS_VERIFY_CTX
structure.
.Pp
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_set_flags
returns the flags passed via parameter
.Fa f .
.Pp
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_add_flags
returns the flags of the context after the ones passed via parameter
.Fa f
are added to it.
.Pp
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_set0_data ,
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_set0_imprint ,
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_set0_store ,
and
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_set0_certs
return 1 if the value could be successfully set and 0 in case of any
error.
.Pp
The deprecated functions
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_set_data ,
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_set_imprint ,
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_set_store ,
.Xr TS_VERIFY_CTX_set_certs 3
return the parameter the user passes via parameter
.Em bio ,
.Fa hexstr ,
.Fa s
or
.Fa certs .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr OSSL_ESS_check_signing_certs 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_set0_data ,
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_set0_imprint ,
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_set0_store ,
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_set0_certs
replace the functions
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_set_data ,
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_set_imprint ,
.Fn TS_VERIFY_CTX_set_store ,
.Xr TS_VERIFY_CTX_set_certs 3
that were deprecated in OpenSSL 3.4.0.
.Pp
The spelling of
.Xr TS_VERIFY_CTX_set_certs 3
was corrected in OpenSSL 3.0.0. The misspelled version
.Xr TS_VERIFY_CTS_set_certs 3
has been retained for compatibility reasons, but it is deprecated in
OpenSSL 3.0.0.
